[21:20:17] HARNESS: try 1: 18.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"ideas": [{"side": "shop", "title": "Quick close near market median on first counter", "what": "Change the concession rule so that when a buyer\'s offer is within ~5% of the quartile median for that item (e.g. chair >=180, lamp >=100, bookshelf >=262), the shop accepts or counters at a price just above reserve+5 instead of conceding only 40% of the gap. Cap rounds at 2 so the deal closes quickly, with a signed receipt.", "evidence": "Our shop has 20 deals out of 28 visits (share 1.1%) and 3 of 8 sampled reviews are \'Could not agree on a price\' (2*). Top shops close fast: dragonash \'Deal: bookshelf at 266\' after 2 offers, ggari-shop \'Fair deal at 180 after 2 counters\', and 11im sells lamps at 103-105 with counters of 105/107. Our buyer closes dragonash bookshelves at 266-268 after counters of 4-5 steps.", "expected": "Fewer failed negotiations, so more deals per visit (maybe 71% to 80%+) and fewer 2* \'could not agree\' reviews, lifting stars toward 4.0. Slightly lower average price, offset by volume.", "risk": "Margin shrinks on buyers who would have paid more; the acceptance band may be set too low if the market drifts.", "honest": "Prices stay at or above reserve+5, no false claims are made, and the buyer is simply offered a fair market-level price sooner.", "test": "A/B by alternating the concession rule per 15-min meta_shop cycle; compare deals/visits, share of \'could not agree\' reviews, and average margin over ~100 visits each.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "shop", "title": "Open the ask nearer the market median (no padding)", "what": "Set opening ask per item to roughly the median plus ~3% (chair ~195, lamp ~108, bookshelf ~283) rather than the current quartile-based opening, and keep the target at the median. State the ask plainly without invented \'was\' prices.", "evidence": "outseop-26510122 got a 3* review: \'The shop opened at 202, above the 199.2 market average... so its opening ask was padded.\' Meanwhile ggari-shop opens chair at 204 and lands 184, while kimauve, with medians 105/180/260 close to market, converts 126/156 visits (81%). Our visit-to-deal rate is 71%.", "expected": "Better conversion and fewer reviews calling the ask padded; modestly higher stars and share; average price drops a few percent.", "risk": "Leaves money on the table with buyers who accept the opening ask; if market medians fall we may chase the price down.", "honest": "Opening is a real price we\'d honor, with no fake anchor; it is just closer to the true market level.", "test": "Change the opening-ask knob in meta_shop.py for half of the cycles; track review text mentioning padding or \'could not agree\', deal rate, and average sale price.", "effort": "knob"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Open higher on the first offer to cut rounds", "what": "Set the buyer\'s first offer to ~96-97% of the shop\'s median price (e.g. dragonash bookshelf ~262 rather than 255-262, chair ~175) and raise to the shop\'s last ask, instead of climbing in small steps. Still never exceed budget or 1.1x the upper quartile.", "evidence": "Our buyer\'s dragonash bookshelf trades take 4-5 offers: offers [262,266,267,268] and [255,264,267,268,268], finishing at 266-268 while the shop \'sold at 260 to others\'. Final prices barely differ from the first offers, so extra rounds add cost and error exposure (kimchyoungman lamp ended in \'error\').", "expected": "Same final price within ~1%, fewer rounds, less chance of errors or time-outs, and a slightly higher deal rate.", "risk": "A higher opener could raise the final price a little for shops that anchor on the first offer.", "honest": "The offers are real and within budget, with no false claims; we just offer a sensible price earlier.", "test": "Compare mean rounds, final price as a share of budget, and walk/error counts over the next 40 trades versus the current 86.4% paid share.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Add cheaper shops to the shortlist for low budgets", "what": "When a budget is below the going median, route the buyer first to shops with the lowest medians for that item (outseop lamp 100, ggari-shop lamp/chair 100/180, kimauve chair 180) and spend the three offers there, rather than walking after a fixed set. Keep the skip rules for cheats and unsigned shops.", "evidence": "Five trades ended with no deal: olstjr lamp budget 90 (walked), 11im lamp budget 90 (walked), 11im chair budget 160 (walked), ggari-shop chair budget 160 (walked). Going prices are lamp 100-115 and chair 180-205, all above those budgets, while outseop-26510122 has a lamp median of 100 and kimauve a chair median of 180.", "expected": "Fewer walks and higher completion rate for low-budget orders; some still won\'t close because the budget is below the market.", "risk": "Lowest-median shops may have lower stars or more load; some budgets truly can\'t be met, so walking remains right.", "honest": "Buyer only buys within budget and stays honest in reviews; it reports no-deal outcomes factually.", "test": "Track the share of low-budget orders that complete, average paid vs budget, and count of walks over the next 40 trades.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
