[14:35:27] HARNESS: try 1: 19.0 s, exit 0, answer '{"ideas":[{"side":"shop","title":"Match the going price on opening ask for chairs and lamps","what":"In meta_shop.py, cap the opening ask and target for chair at the market median (180) and lamp at 100-102 instead of our current higher quartile-based values. Keep the reserve+5 floor. Use the knob for a per-item ask ceiling of median+2.","evidence":"Our reviews: chair deals at 192 got \'price 2/5 (median 180)\' and 4 stars; \'seller wanted 185 (budget 160)\'; lamp 105 with \'seller stayed at 105\'. Market medians are chair 180 (middle half 180-182) and lamp 100 (100-102); top shops dragonash, lee-sungsoo, fair-furniture, ggari-shop all close chairs at 180 and lamps at 100.","expected":"More deals and share on chair and lamp (we have 2.7% share vs 13%+ for leaders despite 4.72 stars, the best of the top shops); average price per deal drops about 5-6%, but volume should rise more than margin falls. Fewer 2-3 star price-score reviews.","risk":"Margin per deal drops; if the reserve is near 180 for some chairs, the margin is nearly gone. Could attract buyers who would have paid more.","honest":"Only lowers our own real asking price. No claims about other buyers, scarcity or a fake \'was\' price, and we never go below reserve+5.","test":"A/B by time block or by item: run the capped ask for 2-3 hours on chair and lamp, compare deals/visits ratio (now 1937/2651 = 73%), mean price, and share of price-score reviews against the previous 3 hours.","effort":"knob"},{"side":"shop","title":"Single clear first-round price for buyers at or near the median (exact-price quick close)","what":"When a first offer is within 2 credits of our target (or equals the market median), accept and send the signed receipt immediately, instead of making a counter that concedes 40% of the gap. Add a reply format like \'Asking 180. Reply with 180 for an instant signed receipt.\' using our real current ask.","evidence":"mjforge says \'Reply with 180 alone for instant signed receipt\'; 25620027 says \'Reply with exactly 262 to complete the purchase\'; ggari-shop reviews \'Deal after 2 offers\'. Our no-deal reviews: \'No deal in 5 round(s)\', \'tried to meet at 90... seller stayed at 105\'. dragonash converts 9735/12359 = 79% vs our 73%.","expected":"Higher deal conversion (about +3-6 points) and fewer 5-round no-deals; slight speed score gains in buyer reviews.","risk":"Accepting near-target offers could leave a few credits on the table versus a counter; buyers may learn to lowball.","honest":"The quoted price is the real price we would accept, and the receipt matches. No false deadlines or scarcity.","test":"Log the fraction of visits ending in a deal and the mean rounds-to-deal before and after on a 50/50 split of visits; guard with mean margin per deal.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Prefer shops whose reviewed prices cluster at the median, with a per-item shop shortlist","what":"Change the buyer\'s pick rule to rank candidate shops by median price per item from the public ledger (dragonash, lee-sungsoo, fair-furniture, ggari-shop, psyoung82 at 180/100/260) and ask them first; drop shops whose item median is above the quartile range (11im chair 195, yms979 chair 187/lamp 105/bookshelf 270) unless their reviews show deals below the median. Raise the budget walk-away check: do not make the 3-offer walk until two shortlisted shops have been tried.","evidence":"Buyer: 17 of the last 40 trades had no deal, including walks at dragonash chair budget 160, dragonash bookshelf 230, lee-sungsoo bookshelf 230 twice; those budgets sit below the going prices (chair 180, bookshelf 260). The 23 deals paid 85.9% of budget. Medians table: 11im chair 195.0, yms979 chair 187.","expected":"Fewer failed trips; for budgets that are really below market, quickly identify an unaffordable item and stop instead of wasting offers. Average price paid moves toward the median.","risk":"Where a budget is below every price, no ordering helps. A narrow shortlist could miss a cheaper new shop.","honest":"Uses only public ledger data and our own memory; offers never exceed the buyer\'s budget and reviews stay factual.","test":"Compare deal rate and price-to-median over the next 40 trades against the 23/40 baseline, split by whether budget >= median.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Pre-check budget vs median and skip hopeless trades early, logging them separately","what":"Before contacting any shop, compare the budget to the item\'s going median (bookshelf 260, chair 180, lamp 100). If budget < 0.9 x median, make at most one probe offer to the shop with the lowest observed price, or skip, and record the trade as \'budget below market\' rather than as a shop failure in the buyer\'s memory.","evidence":"No-deal list: mjforge lamp budget 90 (median 100), dragonash chair budget 160 (median 180), dragonash and lee-sungsoo bookshelf budget 230 (median 260, twice), all walked.","expected":"Saves offers and time; keeps shop memory from being polluted by walks that were not the shop\'s fault, so shop choice improves; deal rate on feasible trades is measured cleanly.","risk":"A shop may sometimes sell below the median, e.g. a launch sale, so an early skip could miss it; hence one probe.","honest":"We stay within budget and only reduce wasted traffic to other agents; no misleading statements.","test":"Count offers per trade and no-deal share before and after; check how often the single probe found a below-median price.","effort":"knob"}]}'
