; small per-deal margin loss offset by volume; share up from 2.5%.", "risk": "If reserve is near 180 for chairs, margin per deal is thin.", "honest": "Prices are our true prices, set from observed market data; no fake \'was\' price.", "test": "Knob change for one item for 3h windows; compare deals/visit and avg stars against the previous window.", "effort": "knob"}, {"side": "shop", "title": "Verifiable receipt and review-friendly deal text", "what": "In the deal message, include a plain factual line: item, agreed price, \'signed by this shop, matches the agreement\', and the receipt number. Do not ask for stars, only an honest review as now.", "evidence": "Positive reviews quote exactly these facts: \'Receipt verified locally\', \'receipt matches the agreement\', \'signed receipt matched the deal\' (dragonash, lee-sungsoo, yms979). Our reviews mention \'A receipt was received\' but score 3*.", "expected": "Buyer-side review templates check receipt match; clearer text may move 3* to 4-5* and lift average stars.", "risk": "Little effect if buyer scoring is mostly price and offer-count driven.", "honest": "Only restates true facts about the receipt; does not request or condition any rating.", "test": "Compare star distribution of reviews for deals before and after the text change over about 500 deals each.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Walk-away fix: one early final-price probe, then switch shop", "what": "When the first ask is above budget (and the gap is over 15%), send one offer at budget, and if the shop\'s reply does not drop below budget, walk at once and go to the next-ranked shop at or below the going median, rather than making three offers. Prefer shops with ledger history of one-offer closes (dragonash, ggari-shop, psyoung82) for budgets at or above the median.", "evidence": "Buyer: 11 of 40 no-deal, including \'ggari-shop chair budget 225 REJECTED\' and \'fair-furniture lamp budget 90 walked\', \'dragonash chair budget 160 walked\'. Medians are 100 lamp and 180 chair, so budgets of 90 and 160 are below every shop. Rejections at ggari-shop with budget 225-250 look like a protocol error, since its replies say \'reply ok and the signed receipt comes back\'.", "expected": "Fewer wasted offers, and the 2 rejected tasks at ggari-shop could convert; deal rate up from 29/40; pay-to-budget ratio stays around 82%.", "risk": "Switching shops early may skip a shop that would have conceded with a third offer.", "honest": "Buyer only bids within its budget and writes factual reviews; no pressure claims.", "test": "Replay the last 40 trades: count how many no-deals fall under the new rule, and for ggari-shop log the rejected message and whether replying \'ok\' exactly as instructed fixes it.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
