[23:39:15] HARNESS: try 1: 20.5 s, exit 0, answer '{"ideas":[{"side":"shop","title":"Price-and-budget-aware review line in the receipt message","what":"Change the post-deal thank-you so it states only verifiable facts the way top-rated shops\' reviews do: item, asked price, paid price, number of offers, and \'signed receipt matches the deal\'. Keep the honest-review request neutral, with no star wording. The aim is that buyers\' auto-generated reviews quote concrete facts instead of generic phrases.","evidence":"11im (4.59 stars) and fair-furniture (4.61) have reviews like \'Bought chair at agreed price 195.0, within budget 225; receipt matches item and task\' and \'Deal at 260 after 1 offer(s); signed receipt matched the agreed price\'. Our reviews are the generic \'Receipt verified locally; fair price 265 within budget.\' and we have 4.5 stars.","expected":"Slightly better review quality and a modest star gain (4.5 toward 4.6), which helps review-based buyer selection and share (currently 2.5%).","risk":"Reviews are written by buyer agents, so the effect may be small. Extra text could also slow replies.","honest":"Only true facts about the deal are stated. Reviews are neither conditioned on nor paid for, and the review request stays neutral.","test":"Compare the average stars and the share of reviews that mention the offer count or the budget, 24h before and after the change, using the market\'s review feed for our shop.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"shop","title":"Close at the ask when a buyer is within a few credits, without a haggling round","what":"Add a rule: if the first offer is within about 3-5% of the target and not below reserve+5, accept at once and issue the signed receipt at the offered price (or the target if it is lower). Also state the exact price to reply with (\'Reply with exactly N for a signed receipt\'), which is the format other shops use.","evidence":"dragonash closes \'in one offer\' with 11773 deals out of 14938 visits (79% conversion). Our conversion is 2252/3041 (74%), and 11im is at 65%. One of our reviews is 3* \'Seller would not meet budget\'. fair-furniture\'s \'asking price: 265\' replies are dropping out of the buyer\'s walks (our buyer walked 5 times on fair-furniture bookshelf at budget 230).","expected":"Conversion up about 2-4 points and fewer 3* reviews from budget mismatches, with a small margin cost.","risk":"Gives up a few credits on offers that would have risen. Could drift below the market median if the threshold is too loose.","honest":"Price never goes below reserve+5 and no false claim is made. The exact-price instruction is true.","test":"A/B by visit parity for 24h: compare deals/visit and average price/target on both arms.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Blacklist or deprioritise shops that repeatedly end in a walk for a given item and budget band","what":"Extend the buyer\'s memory with a key of (shop, item, budget band). After two walks on that key, skip that shop for that item and budget band for several hours and pick the next shop by reviews. Retry later because prices move.","evidence":"\'17 without a deal: fair-furniture bookshelf budget 230 (walked) x5, ggari-shop chair budget 160 (walked)\'. fair-furniture opens at 265 and ggari-shop says \'no shop here may sign below\' 260 for bookshelf, so a budget of 230 can\'t be met. Our buyer completed only 23 of 40 trades.","expected":"Fewer wasted trades; deal rate for the buyer up from 57% toward 70%+. Where no shop is reachable, the budget is simply not spent.","risk":"May skip a shop that would later lower its price. The cooldown has to expire.","honest":"Uses the buyer\'s own honest history. It never offers above budget, never pays above the cap and never lies to shops.","test":"Count repeated (shop, item, budget) walks and the deal rate over the next 40 trades versus the current 23/40.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Shop for budget-tight orders at the cheapest quartile shops: add a price-ceiling prefilter","what":"Before starting a negotiation, compare the budget with each shop\'s observed opening ask and median for the item. Only visit shops whose median is at or below the budget plus the expected concession. If none qualifies, try the lowest-median shop first (corner-store, psyoung82, dragonash at lamp 100) instead of the most-reviewed shop. Use the stated price format (\'Reply with exactly N\').","evidence":"Going prices: bookshelf median 260 (middle half 260-264), yet the buyer\'s budget was 230 in repeated walks. 11im\'s bookshelf median is 270 and \'corner-store says: Deal: lamp at 107\' while others say 100. Several shops accept exact-ask replies, and the quartile band is narrow (260-264), so shops differ by only a few credits.","expected":"Fewer fruitless approaches and a higher deal rate, with paid price staying near 84% of budget or lower.","risk":"The market is narrow-priced (260-264), so the benefit is small when the budget is far below the median; unreachable orders will still end without a deal.","honest":"Uses public price data and the buyer\'s own memory. Offers stay at or under budget and no claims are made.","test":"Per-trade log of shops visited before closing. Compare walks per trade and the share of paid/budget over 40 trades before and after.","effort":"small code"}]}'
