: "Speed sub-score rises from 3-4/5 to 5/5, which gives about +0.3 stars per deal. It also lowers the walk-away rate; one 2* review was \'couldn\'t reach agreement\' at a budget of 185.", "risk": "Some buyers who would have paid more are lost, and buyers who offer low may walk if the first counter is too firm.", "honest": "The final price is true: we state it only when it really is the lowest we will sign, and we never sell below reserve + 5.", "test": "Compare average offers per deal, speed sub-score and the walked fraction for 24h of the new rule against the previous day or a parallel split.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "shop", "title": "Accept a budget offer that is at or above reserve + 5", "what": "When a buyer says their budget (or offers) is within the reserve + 5 margin, close at that offer rather than refusing. Concretely, drop the rule that waits for the target when the buyer is already at the floor and has made two offers. The 2* review case was a buyer with a budget of 185 whom we had come down to but did not close.", "evidence": "2* review: \'Shop came down to my budget of 185 but we couldn\'t reach agreement on final price.\' Visits are 3758 vs 2835 deals (75% conversion), against dragonash at 79% and ggari-shop at 78%.", "expected": "Raises conversion by 1-3 points, removes 2* reviews and lifts stars; share rises with deals.", "risk": "Slightly lower average price on some deals; a code error could let an offer through below reserve + 5.", "honest": "The reserve + 5 floor stays and a deal is only signed at the price the buyer actually offered.", "test": "Log refused offers that were at or above reserve + 5 before and after the change, and compare conversion and 1-2* review counts over 24h.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Reopen a walk case with a second shop within budget", "what": "When the budget is below every shop price, do not walk after three offers at the same shop. Make the third offer at the best other shop below the upper quartile, and for chairs and lamps try a shop whose median is at the market median (dragonash, ggari-shop, cheapest-in-town) instead of walking from the same one. Only raise by 40% of the gap per offer and never exceed the budget.", "evidence": "Our buyer: \'3 without a deal: fair-furniture chair budget 160 (walked); nocha12 lamp budget 90 (walked); ggari-shop lamp budget 90 (walked)\'. These budgets (160, 90, 90) are below the going floor of 180 and 100, and ggari-shop states \'no shop here may sign below the market floor\'. Repeating offers there cannot succeed.", "expected": "Avoids wasted offers (about 7% of trades) and time. It will not create deals below the floor, but it turns lost visits into fewer wasted calls; no change in average pay (84% of budget).", "risk": "Extra calls to other shops cost time and can look like overload if not rate-limited.", "honest": "No budget is exceeded and no false claims are made. The buyer simply stops calling a shop that has said it cannot sell at that price, and writes factual reviews.", "test": "Count wasted offers per walked trade and the share of trades with no deal across 40 trades before and after. Success means fewer offers per walk and the same or higher deal rate.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
