rket middle half is 180-184 and 100-103, so a tight band; our reviews show asks like 275 and 192 above the band.", "expected": "Higher share on lamp/chair from buyers that skip shops above the upper quartile; slightly lower margin per deal, more volume (our share is only 2.5% vs 12% for dragonash).", "risk": "Margin lost if our reserve cost is close to 100/180; invites price-only buyers.", "honest": "Quotes are true prices we actually charge; floor/reserve rules intact.", "test": "Compare visits-to-deals and share per item type before/after on the next two meta_shop cycles; check average paid vs reserve.", "effort": "knob"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Retry shops that rejected us, with a first offer nearer the going median", "what": "When a buyer task ends with no deal and the budget is at or above the going median, make the final (third) offer exactly at the market median and, if a shop\'s ask is within the middle half, accept the shop\'s counter instead of walking. Also stop repeating the same failed shop+item+budget: after a walk at fair-furniture bookshelf 230, do not revisit it with the same budget; choose another shop whose median is at or below our budget.", "evidence": "Buyer last 40: 10 no-deals, including fair-furniture bookshelf budget 230 walked twice (identical case), and bookshelf median is 260 so a 230 budget is below every price. Others: myeonggi chair 205 and lamp 105 were TASK_STATE_REJECTED; inextro chair budget 160 below the 180 median.", "expected": "Fewer wasted turns; deal rate up from 75% toward 85%+; average paid stays well under budget (currently 83%).", "risk": "Skipping low-budget tasks may leave some tasks unfulfilled; paying near median costs more on some deals.", "honest": "Offers never exceed the budget; no false claims to shops; reviews stay factual.", "test": "Log walk reasons per task for 40 trades; compare deal rate and paid/budget ratio before and after, and count repeated (shop, item, budget) failures.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "shop", "title": "Reference signed-receipt and fee transparency in the first quote", "what": "Put the factual receipt line in the opening ask (item, exact price, signed receipt, no added fees, \'send your offer\'), and in the closing message include the price paid and the budget-independent facts so buyers can write the specific review style the top shops get (price, offers count, receipt matched). Do not ask for stars.", "evidence": "Top-rated shops\' deal messages state facts the buyers echo: dragonash \'Closed in four offers. Your receipt is signed by the shop, so this deal counts\'; fair-furniture and mjforge reviews quote \'opened at 189, deal after 6 offers; signed receipt matched\'; cheapest-in-town \'Zero added fees; your signed receipt records this exact item, price and task\'. fair-furniture stars 4.61 and 11im 4.59 vs ours 4.51.", "expected": "Reviews with concrete verifiable details; stars +0.03-0.08 and higher trust for buyers choosing by reviews and ledger; Round 2 counts only signed receipts so stating this helps.", "risk": "Longer messages may confuse an 8B model; wording that sounds like pressure on reviews.", "honest": "States only true facts about the deal and receipt; keeps the existing honest-review request without conditioning or rewarding it.", "test": "Compare review text specificity and mean stars over the next 500 deals against the prior 500.", "effort": "knob"}]}'
