gets 160/230, showing budget-limited buyers walk when the shop holds. Market medians 180/260 are above those budgets, so only the reserve decides whether a sale is possible.", "expected": "Recovers a share of the ~24% of visits that end without a deal (4107 visits vs 3116 deals); modest gain in deals and share, mixed effect on price.", "risk": "If reserve+5 exceeds those budgets there is nothing to recover; buyers can learn to lowball.", "honest": "Respects the reserve and uses the buyer\'s own stated budget; no false claims.", "test": "Log no-deal reasons by (buyer budget, our floor). Count how many lost visits had a final offer >= reserve+5 and compare deals/visits before and after the change.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "shop", "title": "Plain-fact receipt line to speed reviewers\' trust", "what": "Replace the generic \'honest review\' request with a short factual receipt line that mirrors what reviewers cite: \'Deal: <item> at <price> after <n> offers. Signed receipt attached; it records this exact item and price.\' Include the offer count and the exact price, no stars request beyond \'leave an honest review.\'", "evidence": "Positive reviews cite exactly these facts: ggari-shop \'Deal at 180 for a chair (asked 184) after 2 offers, signed receipt\'; fair-furniture \'deal after 4 offers; signed receipt matched\'. Ours: \'market signature validation pending\' appears in several 5* reviews, hinting buyers cannot confirm the signature quickly.", "expected": "Reviews that state a fair price and match, helping buyers who pick by reviews; stars from 4.51 toward 4.6 (fair-furniture 4.61) and slightly better selection.", "risk": "Little effect if buyers do not read the text; small.", "honest": "States only true facts about the deal; asks for an honest review without conditioning anything.", "test": "Compare average stars and the share of reviews mentioning a matched receipt over the next 500 deals vs the previous 500.", "effort": "knob"}, {"side": "buyer", "title