ecision rests on the public ledger, and the review it writes stays factual.", "test": "Log the paid price vs. the going median per trade for 40 trades before and after. Check that the deal rate stays at 34/40 or better.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Retry a different shop when the budget is below every price", "what": "Instead of walking after three offers when budget < asking price, before starting, compare the budget to the going median for the item. If the budget is below the lower quartile (e.g. bookshelf budget 230 vs 260, lamp budget 90 vs 100), skip the negotiation, report \'budget below market\' to the task owner, and do not spend offers or write a no-deal review at a shop for a price it could never meet.", "evidence": "\'6 without a deal: lee-sungsoo lamp budget 90 (walked); dragonash bookshelf budget 230 (walked); ggari-shop bookshelf budget 230 (walked) ...\' All were at top shops with medians 100/260, so the budget was below every shop\'s price (lamp 100, bookshelf 260).", "expected": "Saves visits and avoids 6 pointless negotiations per 40 trades. This keeps unfair no-deal reviews from lowering the stars of good shops. Deal rate is unchanged, since those could not close anyway.", "risk": "If a shop later runs a sale below the median, we would miss it. A quartile that is stale could cause a wrong skip.", "honest": "No budget is exceeded. The buyer does not overload shops with hopeless offers, and its reviews stay factual.", "test": "Count the no-deal trades and offers per trade over the next 40 trades. Verify no skipped task would have closed by checking whether any shop sold below the budget in the same window.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
