ely. Going prices have middle halves of only 260-264, 180-182 and 100-100.","expected":"Fewer walk-aways and fewer \'price 3/5\' reviews. Average price falls a little (about 1-2%), but deals and stars rise, so share goes up.","risk":"We give up margin of about 5 credits on each bookshelf that would have sold at 265. If the market median rises we would underprice.","honest":"We quote true prices and never go below reserve+5. We make no claims about a \'was\' price.","test":"Run an A/B by item on meta_shop.py. Compare conversion, average price, and the share of reviews with price 3/5 or lower over about 500 visits per arm.","effort":"knob"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Start higher and jump to the shop\'s flat ask when it has been flat","what":"If a shop repeats the same ask on two consecutive replies (the ask is its floor), stop the 40%-of-gap raises. Offer that ask directly if it is at or below the median plus 1-2% and within budget. Otherwise walk at once.","evidence":"Our buyer paid 270 at psyoung82 for a bookshelf, with asks [270 x7] and offers [258, 262, ..., 270], while the same item sold at 260 to others. The ask never moved, so 6 to 7 offers were wasted. Reviews of other shops show \'deal after 7 offers\' scoring 3*.","expected":"Fewer offers per deal. Faster deals improve our speed ratings and save time. The buyer should also stop paying 270 at shops where 260 is the going price.","risk":"We may skip a shop that would have conceded after a few more offers.","honest":"We make real offers within budget and do not mislead the seller. We only stop early when the evidence says the price is fixed.","test":"Track the average number of offers per deal and the average price paid against the median over 40 trades. Count walks caused by the new rule.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Blacklist shops that repeat a flat ask above the median","what":"Record the final price against the public median per shop and item. Add a per-item penalty for shops that sold above median+3 (psyoung82 bookshelf at 270) and prefer shops with a proven median price (ggari-shop, fair-furniture, cheapest-in-town) for items where we have a tight budget.","evidence":"psyoung82 bookshelf was bought four times at 270 although it sold at 260 to others. Budget-90 lamp tasks walked at ggari-shop, dragonash and cheapest-in-town, where the floor is 100 (ggari-shop \'no shop here may sign below it\').","expected":"Cuts the average paid price by about 3% on bookshelves, and saves visits on tasks that cannot succeed.","risk":"Over-concentrating on a few shops may leave us with fewer options if they go down. The penalty needs to expire.","honest":"Purely our own purchase memory and public ledger data. No fake claims about other buyers.","test":"Compare the average price/median ratio and the % of budget used on the next 40 trades. Count the walks where the budget is below the known floor and see whether we skip them earlier.","effort":"small code"}]}'
