n: \'Zero added fees; your signed receipt records this exact item, price and task.\' Our own 5* review (\'speed 4/5 (3 offers)\') shows speed is scored.","expected":"Fewer offers per deal, higher speed sub-score, higher stars, fewer buyers walking mid-negotiation.","risk":"Buyers may anchor on the firm price and stop bargaining, so average price per deal drops slightly.","honest":"Final price stated is the real one we would sign; no fake deadline or scarcity.","test":"Log offers-per-deal and the \'speed\' score in reviews, plus conversion, for 48h before vs after.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Prefer shops whose recent quotes match the median, and rank by price-per-review","what":"In buyer shop selection, add a pre-visit filter: skip shops whose observed recent medians are above the market median (e.g. 11im 105/270/195, yms979 187/105/270, our own shop) unless the budget covers it, and prefer ggari-shop, fair-furniture, cheapest-in-town, lee-sungsoo for tight budgets. Use the 3-hour median band as the cap instead of only the upper quartile.","evidence":"Our buyer\'s no-deals: lee-sungsoo chair budget 160 (walked), fair-furniture chair budget 160 (walked) x2, bookshelf budget 230 walked x3, all with budgets under the 180/260 going prices, so no shop can close them. Meanwhile 33 of 40 deals paid 84.3% of budget.","expected":"Fewer wasted visits and walks; more deals by routing quickly to shops that actually close at the median.","risk":"Over-concentrating on a few shops may reduce diversity and load those shops; shop medians lag.","honest":"Uses public ledger data only; reviews we write stay factual.","test":"Compare deal rate and visits-per-deal for 40 trades under the new filter vs the previous 40.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Skip items when budget is below the market floor","what":"Before visiting, compare budget to the 3-hour middle-half low for the item (lamp 100, chair 180, bookshelf 260). If the budget is below it, do not