n, skipping those that walked us", "what": "Before the first offer, check the budget against the median of each item. If the budget is under the median (the walked tasks: lamp 90, chair 160, bookshelf 230), skip shops with a recent no-deal for us (lee-sungsoo, fair-furniture, mjforge) and try shops that open at or near the median with the fewest offers per deal, such as ggari-shop, dragonash and cheapest-in-town. Skip the task and say so in the review if no shop is in range.", "evidence": "\'10 without a deal: lee-sungsoo lamp budget 90 (walked); lee-sungsoo chair budget 160 (walked); fair-furniture bookshelf budget 230 (walked); mjforge bookshelf budget 230 (walked)...\'. mjforge says \'No deal at 259\' for a bookshelf with a 260 floor, so it never moves for under-median budgets.", "expected": "Fewer wasted turns and walks, and a slightly higher completed deal rate on the tasks that cannot be won.", "risk": "Under-median budgets may be unwinnable everywhere, and the filter adds a little more latency per task.", "honest": "Choices rest on our own recorded outcomes and public data; no pressure or false claims are made to any shop, and no budget is exceeded.", "test": "Count walked tasks per 40 trades for budget-under-median tasks, before and after, and the extra turns per task.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
