": "Going prices: bookshelf 260 (middle half 260-264), chair 180 (180-181), lamp 100 (100-102). Our reviews show deals at chair 185 and bookshelf 265, with review lines \'price 4/5 (median 185)\' and \'(median 265)\' while the market median is 180 and 260, so we lose the price star and sit 5 above where top shops (ggari-shop, fair-furniture, lee-sungsoo, cheapest-in-town) close.", "expected": "Price sub-score 4/5 to 5/5 in reviews, stars toward 4.55+, higher win rate against buyers who skip shops above the upper quartile; margin per deal drops about 2%, volume should more than offset it.", "risk": "Thin margins; if reserve is near 100/180/260 there is little room, and others may undercut further.", "honest": "Only lowers prices to the real market level; never sells below reserve; no fake \'was\' price.", "test": "Run for 3 hours on one item (chair) vs control items; compare deals/visit, average price, and the price sub-score in reviews.", "effort": "knob"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Stop re-visiting shops our buyer repeatedly walks from; use per-shop budget fit memory", "what": "Add to the buyer\'s own memory a record (shop, item, budget bucket, outcome). Before choosing, skip a shop for that item when it walked at a similar budget two or more times in the last N trades, and prefer shops whose medians are at or under the budget (ggari-shop, fair-furniture, cheapest-in-town, 25620027 quote 180/100/260).", "evidence": "Our buyer: 11 of last 40 trades had no deal, and lee-sungsoo appears repeatedly as walked: \'lee-sungsoo bookshelf budget 230 (walked); lee-sungsoo lamp budget 90 (walked); lee-sungsoo lamp budget 90 (walked); lee-sungsoo bookshelf budget 230 (walked)\'. Medians at lee-sungsoo are 260 and 100, above those budgets.", "expected": "Deal rate from 29/40 (72%) toward 80%+, fewer wasted trades; if budget is below every market price, skip faster rather than three offers.", "risk": "Overfitting to a short history, and a shop may change prices; budgets under t