d memory could overfit; budgets below market price will remain unsellable and must not be forced above budget.", "honest": "The buyer never exceeds the budget or the 1.1x quartile cap and writes factual reviews.", "test": "Log walk-aways per (shop, item, budget band) for 40 trades before and after; compare deal rate and paid-to-budget ratio.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "shop", "title": "Include a verifiable share of the real recorded outcome in our closing message", "what": "In the deal message, state facts we can show: item, agreed price, number of offers, and that the receipt is signed. For example \'Deal: chair at 181. Closed in 2 offers. Signed receipt matches.\' This mimics dragonash\'s and 25620027\'s closers that review writers quote back, and so produces specific reviews. Keep the honest-review request without conditions or rewards.", "evidence": "Reviews of dragonash and 25620027 repeat the exact fields from the shop\'s message: \'deal after 2 offers; signed receipt matched the deal\', \'Completed in 7 buyer offer(s). Seller-signed receipt matches the agreed price.\' Our own best review (5*) says \'its ask went 192 -> 185 ... receipt shows exactly the agreed price and is signed\', showing buyers score what they can verify.", "expected": "Slightly higher average stars (ours 4.49 vs fair-furniture 4.57 and ggari-shop 4.55) because buyers have concrete facts to check and reward.", "risk": "Low. A model-written message could misstate the number of offers, so the numbers must come from code, not from the Llama 8B.", "honest": "Every figure is generated from the actual negotiation record; no claim about other buyers, scarcity or deadlines, and the review request is unconditional.", "test": "Change the template on half of the deals; compare the mean stars and the share of 4-5* reviews.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
