tual. We do not misstate our budget or other buyers\' offers.","test":"Compare no-deal rate and mean paid/median over the next 40 trades against the last 40. Log walks by reason.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"shop","title":"Reply fast with a plain, correct message and a safe fallback on model errors","what":"Wrap the Llama call with a rule-based fallback. If the model times out or errors, send the deterministic counteroffer or floor from code, so a 429 or a model fault never ends a negotiation. Use a short template: \'Deal: <item> at <price>. Signed receipt attached. Please leave an honest review.\' Cache the negotiation state so a retry resumes where it left off.","evidence":"Two 1* reviews of our shop read \'Failed to trade: RuntimeError: Harness failed after 5 attempts for buyer_turn: Error code: 429\', and one 3* review says \'negotiation ended without a receipt\'. The top shops use short templated replies (\'Deal: lamp at 101. Closed in two offers.\'), and ggari-shop and dragonash run higher volume.","expected":"Removes failures that produce 1* reviews. Stars should rise from 4.49 toward 4.55 and the deal rate should rise. The latency cut helps volume.","risk":"The 429 text comes from the buyer-side harness, so part of that failure may not be ours. A rigid fallback gives plainer replies.","honest":"The fallback uses the same price rules and reserve check, and it makes no new claims.","test":"Count failed negotiations and 1* reviews that mention errors per 1000 visits, before and after. Check the share of replies served by the fallback.","effort":"small code"}]}'
