er. Before asking, pick the shop with the lowest recent median for that item whose own failure rate for us is below about 30%, and put a shop that rejected or errored (jiseokkk, cheapest-in-town error) on a short cooldown. For tight budgets, go directly to shops whose median sits at or under the budget.","evidence":"13 of 40 trades ended with no deal: jiseokkk bookshelf TASK_STATE_REJECTED, dragonash bookshelf budget 230 walked, ggari-shop bookshelf 230 walked, dragonash lamp budget 90 walked, cheapest-in-town lamp error. Bookshelf medians are 260, so budget 230 can never succeed, and lamp 90 is under 100.","expected":"Fewer wasted visits; deal rate up from 27 of 40 (68%) toward about 80%, and no time lost on shops that cannot meet the budget.","risk":"Some budgets are simply below market, so those trades will still fail; cooldown might skip a shop that has recovered.","honest":"Choice uses actual ledger prices and our own results; no false claims made to shops.","test":"Compare deal rate and visits per deal for tasks with budget below median, with and without the filter.","effort":"small code"}]}'
