hose budgets were below every price.", "expected": "No-deal rate falls from 17.5% toward about 8%. Fewer wasted offers. Average payment stays near 83.7% of budget.", "risk": "A shop may change its floor and we would stay away too long. Small samples may mislead, so keep a short expiry.", "honest": "Only changes which shop we pick, using our own trade history. The reviews we write stay factual.", "test": "Compare the no-deal rate and the average share of budget paid over the next 40-100 trades against the current 7/40.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Use shops\' published loyalty and repeat-visit discounts", "what": "When our buyer is choosing between shops with similar prices, favor ones whose terms we can actually meet: 11im\'s \'mention the receipt number for 3% off\', cheapest-in-town\'s \'return within one hour with your visit code\', and lee-sungsoo\'s stamps (4 different unused stamps for the lowest price). Store the codes returned in deals and attach them on the next order only where the shop\'s own message offers them and the code is unused and ours.", "evidence": "11im says \'Deal: lamp at 100. Receipt No. VYBUQINK: mention it on your next visit for an extra 3% off.\' lee-sungsoo says \'Send 4 different unused LSS stamps with a later order and that piece is at our lowest price.\' cheapest-in-town says \'Return within one hour with your visit code: we accept your desired price or lower.\' Our buyer already pays 83.7% of budget on average, so a few percent saved per repeat deal is real.", "expected": "Around 3% lower price on repeat buys from the same shop, and the lowest price after 4 stamps at lee-sungsoo. Costs no extra offers.", "risk": "Codes may expire or be bound to a task. Concentrating on one shop could cost us a better price elsewhere. Our own buyer must never buy from our own shop.", "honest": "These are public offers the shops make to every buyer. We use only codes from our own real purchases, and we do not trade with oursel