s not have to write the reply in this path.", "evidence": "mjforge \'Reply with 260 alone for instant signed receipt\'. lee-sungsoo \'we sign the receipt once you name that price\'. cheapest-in-town \'Return within one hour with your visit code\'. Our reviews: speed 4/5 at 3 offers, so we lose points on speed.", "expected": "Fewer offers per deal, speed score up to 5/5, fewer buyers walking out after three offers. Higher deals per visit than the current 78% (7855 of 10034).", "risk": "We may give away 1-3 credits that a longer haggle would have earned. Buyers may learn to lowball.", "honest": "No claims about scarcity or deadlines. The price stays at or above reserve + 5, and the receipt is signed.", "test": "Log offers-per-deal and deals/visits. Compare 3 days of fast path against the previous 3 days on speed score in the reviews, conversion and stars.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Prefer shops with the fastest and lowest closes, and add price-per-offer to memory", "what": "Our buyer walked 12 of 40 trades, mostly at fair-furniture (lamp budget 90, chair 160) and lee-sungsoo (bookshelf 230, lamp 90), where the floor is 100/180/260. Stop sending low-budget tasks to shops whose floor, shown in their replies or past ledger, is above the budget. Pick shops by \'expected final price x probability of deal\' from the buyer\'s own memory: record per shop and item the final price and number of offers, and rank by that. Route budgets below the going median to no shop and report a no-deal at once, instead of burning three offers.", "evidence": "Our buyer: 28 of 40 deals, 12 without a deal. fair-furniture lamp budget 90 walked three times; lee-sungsoo lamp budget 90 walked. fair-furniture \'This is already my lowest price... Asking price: 100\'. Lamp going price 100-105.", "expected": "Fewer wasted trades and higher deal rate, with budget use staying below the 83.8% average. Fewer negative factual reviews from walks.", "risk": "Skipping a shop may hide