iewers then write specific, factual reviews. Our stars 4.5 vs fair-furniture 4.58 and 11im 4.56.","expected":"More specific, factual reviews and a small stars rise (+0.03 to +0.08), helping buyers who choose by review content.","risk":"Minimal; could slightly lengthen messages or have no measurable effect.","honest":"Statements are true and generated from the deal record. It asks for an honest review without conditioning or rewarding it.","test":"Compare mean stars and review-text receipt mentions for deals before/after the template change, or by odd/even deal ids.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"buyer","title":"Walk-away avoidance: pick the shop that closed at budget before","what":"Add a per-shop, per-item memory of recent outcomes at similar budgets (deal/walk and price paid). When the budget is below the going median, rank shops by their past success rate for that budget band and skip shops that walked us twice on that item. Try shops whose reviews show deals near the median first (fair-furniture, ggari, dragonash).","evidence":"Our buyer: 11 of the last 40 trades had no deal; walks were at fair-furniture (bookshelf 230, chair 160), lee-sungsoo (bookshelf 230, chair 160), and mjforge (chair 160). Budgets of 160 for chairs and 230 for bookshelves are well under the 180 and 260 medians, so no shop at median prices will close them.","expected":"Fewer wasted trades (fewer no-deal results), and a deal rate above 29/40; average paid share may rise slightly but deals count for more.","risk":"Over-fitting to a few observations; may skip a shop that would give a deal after a price change.","honest":"Uses only our own trade history and public data; no claims to shops, never above budget.","test":"Track deal rate on trades with budget < 0.9 x median before and after, compared to the previous 40 trades.","effort":"small code"},{"side":"shop","title":"Plain budget-aware price transparency instead of RPS or gimmicks","what":"When the buyer\'s offer is under the floor, state 