ror/reject, immediately re-route the same task to the next-ranked shop whose median is at or below our budget (e.g. fair-furniture, cheapest-in-town, ggari-shop alternates), with a cap of 2 shops per task. Skip shops that rejected or errored on that task.","evidence":"4 of our 6 non-deals are bookshelves at budget 230 or 270 (inextro walked, dragonash error, lee-sungsoo walked, jiseokkk walked, ggari-shop rejected at budget 270), while going bookshelf median is 260 and budget 230 is below every price. The 34/40 deal rate could rise if the budget-aware choice were made earlier.","expected":"Deal rate up from 85% toward 90%+; average paid share of budget stays about 83%.","risk":"Budget 230 is below all market prices, so some tasks are infeasible; extra visits could bump visit counts of rivals.","honest":"We never offer above budget, never exceed the 1.1x quartile cap, and do not overload anyone (max 2 shops, 3 offers each).","test":"Log tasks where budget < median: compare completion rate with and without fallback over the next 100 buyer trades.","effort":"small code"}]}'
