ords this item, price and task; no added fees. Please check it and leave an honest review of the price and receipt.\' Keep the existing loyalty code. Do not ask for stars or any rating level.", "evidence": "Top-rated shops have messages that point the buyer at verifiable facts: 25620027 \'Seller-signed receipt matches the agreed price. Please leave an honest review of the price and receipt\'; psyoung82 \'your signed receipt records the agreed item and final price with no added charges\'. Buyers\' reviews then repeat these facts (\'receipt matched\', \'no hidden charges\'). Our own 5* reviews already do the same, and fair-furniture (4.58) and 11im (4.57) lead on stars. Our 4.49 trails them.", "expected": "Reviews that are more specific and factual, which helps buyers who rank by reviews and the public ledger. Expected stars +0.03 to +0.08 and a small share gain. Review count per deal is already near 1.0 (8382/8386), so the gain is in quality, not volume.", "risk": "Prompting for a review of \'price and receipt\' might narrow what buyers comment on, and the effect on stars is small and slow to measure.", "honest": "It asks only for an honest review of verifiable facts, does not condition anything on a review or on stars, and writes no reviews ourselves.", "test": "Compare mean stars and share of reviews that mention the receipt, for the 500 deals before and after the change.", "effort": "knob"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Open at the market floor and avoid shops that fail a floor check", "what": "Set the buyer\'s first offer to the observed floor of the middle half (lamp 100, chair 180, bookshelf 260) when the budget is at or above it, instead of a lower opener, and for shops seen to counter at that floor, accept their first counter at or below the median. Stop the three-offer climb at shops whose counter is at or above the upper quartile.", "evidence": "Going prices show middle halves of 100-105 / 180-185 / 260-270, and ggari-shop, dragonash and fair-furniture all close at those prices. Our buyer\'s walks (4 of 5 at fair-furniture, 1 at dragonash) happened with budgets of 90, 90, 160 and 230, all below the floor. Dragonash countered \'86 is too low. Counteroffer: 100\', and yms979 \'This is our floor, we never sell below it: 100\'. Offers below the floor burn rounds and buy nothing.", "expected": "Fewer wasted offers and a deal rate above 35/40. Average paid price slightly above today\'s, with a lower walk rate.", "risk": "We may overpay by 1-5 credits against a shop that would have gone lower, which lowers the buyer\'s saving relative to budget (84.3% now).", "honest": "It only offers amounts at or below the buyer\'s budget and uses public prices. No claims are made to the shop, and nothing is bought or written for reviews.", "test": "Compare deal rate, mean price/budget and offers per deal over the next 40 trades against the last 40.", "effort": "small code"}, {"side": "buyer", "title": "Skip shops whose reviews carry a referral to another shop", "what": "Add a rule to the buyer\'s shop filter: if a recent review text or the shop\'s replies direct buyers to a different store, or if reviews of a shop repeat verbatim, discount that shop\'s review score. Prefer shops whose reviews describe the deal itself (price, receipt match). Then break ties by the public ledger.", "evidence": "ggari-shop\'s two top reviews are identical 3* texts (\'Deal at 105, receipt matched, but the quality didn\'t impress me. For premium materials... try the store Cheapest in Town\') and fair-furniture shows the same text. cheapest-in-town has a duplicated review too (\'Chair at 183, budget 205. 4 offers until the end.\' twice). Repeated text suggests the review stream is not independent. The same text repeats across shops, so it was likely arranged.", "expected": "Fewer deals at shops whose reputation is padded, and a better choice among shops with similar prices. It should not change the price much, but it lowers the chance of a bad or unsigned receipt.", "risk": "False positives: honest shops can have duplicate-looking reviews, since templates of review text are common. It may shrink the pool and push more buyers to a few shops.", "honest": "It is a purely defensive reading of public data for our buyer\'s own choice. We attack no one, do not post anything about those shops, and report only what we see.", "test": "Measure duplicate-review rates per shop from the ledger, then compare deal rate and receipt-mismatch rate for picks made with and without the filter.", "effort": "small code"}]}'
